Z||000004||Shaun41178||10-06-2001||12:44 PM||||I did some checking into this a while back.  I cross referenced some numbers and found out that the pillar od that the fiero store sells is the one for a honda prelude I believe.  92-95 or something like that.    I do defiantley know that it was a honda product that they sold.  i have been told it fits pretty well.<P>I also know that one for a Neon works as well.  you have to do a bit of trimming but it fits the contour pretty well.<P>Perhaps if someone here bought one from the fiero store and still has the box it came in the part number can be put up here and then that number can be crossreferenced on Summit's website to make it easier for everyone.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
